# Design: Metal through the host door. The pages spec/core-operations.md and spec/nums.md are the authority; these nodes say what was chosen and why.

n: 5.14.62
name: metal-through-the-door
kind: hub
is: The GPU is reached from Form: a target the processor does not run is a bound blueprint, and what the C header did is a component package over rows of the host.
at: 2026-11-27

n: 5.14.62.1
name: a-target-is-a-bound-blueprint
kind: decision
is: The bootstrap holds no Metal. A code leaf of a target the processor does not run is run by what its blueprint is bound to, given the leaf and the values, whether native names it or a binding holds it. has-target answers for the processor alone, and a target binds the entry to answer for itself.
status: inferred
from: 5.14.60 5.19.37 7.21 5.9.2
conf: mid
why: Run on 2026-11-27 on an M4 Max: the image flow of make check answered the bytes the C dispatch gave for the same five requests, a 65-lane map in both operand orders, the empty vector and two invalid shapes, from a directory holding only the image. The same holds against main's later flow, where an application calls the map inside one search in both operand orders. The bootstrap went from 2,000 lines to 1,906.
flip: A dispatch walked through rows takes about 7.3 ms where the C took 3.6, and a start 22 ms where it took 5. Where that matters the rows can be emitted as moves and a call, or the device and pipeline kept between maps.
limit: Rows exist for Apple's arm64 convention only, so under Rosetta, where the C dispatch ran, has-target now answers no and a map answers no-native. One machine.
at: 2026-11-27

n: 5.14.62.2
name: what-a-dispatch-makes-lies-in-a-room
kind: decision
is: The package host/metal.ck runs a map through seven host functions and 28 Objective-C messages, each a row. Every object it makes is written into a slot of one room as it is made, and let go by a row when the dispatch ends, when a fault leaves it and before the next begins. The two sizes of three words go by reference from that room. The package reaches the host only through seven recipes it is handed.
status: inferred
from: 5.14.62.1 5.14.60
conf: mid
why: By hand on 2026-11-27: a fault raised at the first copy into the buffer came out as itself with all eight slots empty, and a device left in a slot was let go by the next map. The package written as Python by the writer parses.
flip: A host object that must outlive a dispatch, such as a pipeline kept between maps, needs a slot that is not let go at the end.
limit: The fault path is held by no check. The check of the buffer against the allowance takes and gives back a room of that size, which raises the peak the allowance counts. The buffer itself is the host's memory.
at: 2026-11-27

n: 5.14.62.3
name: the-door-is-opened-ahead
kind: decision
is: A map may run while a choice is open. Everything the host is asked by name is asked when the door is opened with no choice open: each function's address, each message's registered name, the pool's class. A dispatch then makes no call of entry 98: it runs machine code through the berth on addresses it holds, reads its operands where they lie in the region, and lets go of all it made before it answers. Entry 98 stays refused under a choice.
status: inferred
from: 5.14.62.2 5.14.60 5.7.3
conf: mid
why: Main's application calls the map inside an all over two operand orders. With lookups made at each call the reply was the fault irreversible; with the door opened ahead the five replies are the bytes the C dispatch gave. By hand, four maps gathered by one all over two choices answered four vectors.
alt: Holding the map back with after, which cannot give its answer to the search that asked. Refusing, which would end the application's flow.
flip: A dispatch that left something standing in the host, such as a pipeline kept between maps, would have to be made before the choice or be refused under it.
limit: That a dispatch leaves nothing behind is the package's own care and no check of the walker: host.run is not refused under a choice. A buffer's bytes in the host are gone when it is let go, yet what the device did meanwhile is not something a fail could have undone.
at: 2026-11-27
